{"schemaVersion":1,"source":"MediaWiki REST revision HTML, sanitized","nodeCount":1164,"content":[{"type":"section","props":{"id":"mwAQ"},"children":[{"type":"p","props":{},"children":[]},"\n\n"]},{"type":"section","props":{"id":"mwBQ"},"children":[{"type":"h2","props":{"id":"Description"},"children":["Description"]},"\n",{"type":"p","props":{},"children":["The ",{"type":"b","props":{},"children":["Overworld"]}," is one of the many realms that was spawned from the seed of Paradise, and is the realm to which the main events of the game's story line take place. It is mainly supposed to be the equivalent to Earth, but certain elements of the realm indicate that the ",{"type":"b","props":{},"children":["Overworld"]}," also shares similarities to what Robloxia is supposed to be, from official Roblox material. "]},"\n\n"]},{"type":"section","props":{"id":"mwCQ"},"children":[{"type":"h2","props":{"id":"Inhabitants"},"children":["Inhabitants"]},"\n",{"type":"p","props":{},"children":["The primary inhabitants of the ",{"type":"b","props":{},"children":["Overworld"]}," are known as humans.",{"type":"sup","props":{},"children":[{"type":"a","props":{"href":"/w/Overworld#cite_note-1"},"children":[{"type":"span","props":{"id":"mwDQ"},"children":[{"type":"span","props":{"id":"mwDg"},"children":["["]},"1",{"type":"span","props":{"id":"mwDw"},"children":["]"]}]}]}]}," Like humans in the real world, the humans of Tower Defense Simulator seem to be the apex species of their world, dominating the globe. Though, whether the humans of Tower Defense Simulator share the same, or similar histories and upbringings of the humans of the real world remains unknown, as the Robloxia-inspired elements of the ",{"type":"b","props":{},"children":["Overworld"]}," could possibly influence elements of humanity. "]},"\n\n",{"type":"p","props":{},"children":["Zombies are another set of beings that inhabit the ",{"type":"b","props":{},"children":["Overworld"]},", they are the undead corpses of humans that have been mutated and animated to life by the effects of ",{"type":"a","props":{"href":"/w/Serum_Zero","title":"Serum Zero"},"children":["Serum Zero"]}," developed by Oasis X Enterprise laboratories.",{"type":"sup","props":{},"children":[{"type":"a","props":{"href":"/w/Overworld#cite_note-2"},"children":[{"type":"span","props":{"id":"mwFQ"},"children":[{"type":"span","props":{"id":"mwFg"},"children":["["]},"2",{"type":"span","props":{"id":"mwFw"},"children":["]"]}]}]}]}," It is unknown when the zombies first started appearing in the ",{"type":"b","props":{},"children":["Overworld"]},", but as of ",{"type":"a","props":{"href":"/w/The_Final_Act_Event","title":"The Final Act Event"},"children":["The Final Act Event"]},", they seem to retain a sizable global population.",{"type":"sup","props":{},"children":[{"type":"a","props":{"href":"/w/Overworld#cite_note-3"},"children":[{"type":"span","props":{"id":"mwGw"},"children":[{"type":"span","props":{"id":"mwHA"},"children":["["]},"3",{"type":"span","props":{"id":"mwHQ"},"children":["]"]}]}]}]}," From certain cinematic material, zombies possess an intelligence of some degree and a drive for self-preservation.",{"type":"sup","props":{},"children":[{"type":"a","props":{"href":"/w/Overworld#cite_note-4"},"children":[{"type":"span","props":{"id":"mwHw"},"children":[{"type":"span","props":{"id":"mwIA"},"children":["["]},"4",{"type":"span","props":{"id":"mwIQ"},"children":["]"]}]}]}]}]},"\n\n",{"type":"p","props":{},"children":["Lesser known entities known as ",{"type":"a","props":{"href":"/w/Pumpkid","title":"Pumpkid"},"children":["Pumpkids"]}," and ",{"type":"a","props":{"href":"/w/Swamper","title":"Swamper"},"children":["Swampers"]},{"type":"sup","props":{},"children":[{"type":"a","props":{"href":"/w/Overworld#cite_note-5"},"children":[{"type":"span","props":{"id":"mwJg"},"children":[{"type":"span","props":{"id":"mwJw"},"children":["["]},"5",{"type":"span","props":{"id":"mwKA"},"children":["]"]}]}]}]}," have been shown to be living in the ",{"type":"b","props":{},"children":["Overworld"]},". It can be assumed that they are each their own separate species of monsters native to the realm, and that there is likely more of them not shown in the game."]},"\n\n"]},{"type":"section","props":{"id":"mwKg"},"children":[{"type":"h2","props":{"id":"Groups"},"children":["Groups"]},"\n",{"type":"p","props":{},"children":["The ",{"type":"a","props":{"href":"/w/T.D.S._Organization","title":"T.D.S. Organization"},"children":["T.D.S. Organization"]}," is the protagonist force in the Tower Defense Simulator story and is a primary faction whose operations are based from the ",{"type":"b","props":{},"children":["Overworld"]},". Their goal is to fight back against the zombies, Molten, ",{"type":"a","props":{"href":"/w/Fallen_(Story)","title":"Fallen (Story)"},"children":["Fallen"]},", and any other force that wishes to pose a threat to humanity and the world. As of the ",{"type":"a","props":{"href":"/w/Null_&_Void_Event","title":"Null & Void Event"},"children":["Null & Void Event"]},", they also worked to secure ",{"type":"a","props":{"href":"/w/God_Cube","title":"God Cube"},"children":["God Cube"]}," fragments, whether it be from within the ",{"type":"b","props":{},"children":["Overworld"]}," or from other realms. But after ",{"type":"a","props":{"href":"/w/Lord_Exo","title":"Lord Exo"},"children":["Lord Exo"]},"'s freedom from the ",{"type":"a","props":{"href":"/w/God_Cube","title":"God Cube"},"children":["God Cube"]},", the ",{"type":"a","props":{"href":"/w/T.D.S._Organization","title":"T.D.S. Organization"},"children":["T.D.S. Organization"]},"'s new focus is trying to limit the damage of the ",{"type":"a","props":{"href":"/w/Meta","title":"Meta"},"children":["Meta"]}," falling apart, and fight back against any destruction that ",{"type":"a","props":{"href":"/w/Lord_Exo","title":"Lord Exo"},"children":["Lord Exo"]}," might cause."]},"\n\n",{"type":"p","props":{},"children":["The ",{"type":"a","props":{"href":"/w/Children_of_Exo","title":"Children of Exo"},"children":["Children of Exo"]}," are a mysterious cult and terrorist organization whose goal is to free ",{"type":"a","props":{"href":"/w/Lord_Exo","title":"Lord Exo"},"children":["Lord Exo"]}," from his prison. As of the ",{"type":"a","props":{"href":"/w/Null_&_Void_Event","title":"Null & Void Event"},"children":["Null & Void Event"]},", they have achieved their goal. They are aligned against the ",{"type":"a","props":{"href":"/w/T.D.S._Organization","title":"T.D.S. Organization"},"children":["T.D.S. Organization"]},"."]},"\n\n",{"type":"p","props":{},"children":["The Dark Sun",{"type":"sup","props":{},"children":[{"type":"a","props":{"href":"/w/Overworld#cite_note-6"},"children":[{"type":"span","props":{"id":"mwPg"},"children":[{"type":"span","props":{"id":"mwPw"},"children":["["]},"6",{"type":"span","props":{"id":"mwQA"},"children":["]"]}]}]}]}," is an enigmatic faction lead by ",{"type":"a","props":{"href":"/w/The_Umbra","title":"The Umbra"},"children":["The Umbra"]},". They had been working in the shadows to retrieve ",{"type":"a","props":{"href":"/w/God_Cube","title":"God Cube"},"children":["God Cube"]}," fragments for their Mistress. Their attempts were thwarted many times by the ",{"type":"a","props":{"href":"/w/T.D.S._Organization","title":"T.D.S. Organization"},"children":["T.D.S. Organization"]},", with ",{"type":"a","props":{"href":"/w/The_Umbra","title":"The Umbra"},"children":["The Umbra"]}," ultimately being defeated at ",{"type":"a","props":{"href":"/w/Totality_Tower","title":"Totality Tower"},"children":["Totality Tower"]},", and the Dark Sun presumably along with her."]},"\n\n"]},{"type":"section","props":{"id":"mwRg"},"children":[{"type":"h2","props":{"id":"Locations"},"children":["Locations"]},"\n",{"type":"div","props":{"id":"ext-interactivenaps-transclusion-1"},"children":[{"type":"div","props":{},"children":[{"type":"div","props":{},"children":[]},{"type":"div","props":{},"children":[{"type"